.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.9.0.0.md:12:This release completes the executor expansion begun in v1.8.0.0 by making `cli-copilot` and `cli-claude-code` available for research iterations and rejecting settings their CLIs do not support. Phase 018 wired `cli-codex` as its only new executor and reserved the two new CLIs in the config enum while rejecting them at load time. The YAML workflow keeps ownership of state, convergence, lifecycle and the reducer, and this release ships as a symmetric pair with `deep-review` v1.6.0.0.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.9.0.0.md:24:- **Cross-CLI delegation is documented as design intent.** Both `SKILL.md` files gain a Cross-CLI Delegation subsection under the Executor Selection Contract. Any CLI executor can shell out to another CLI from its iteration sandbox, while self-recursive invocation is forbidden and each individual CLI skill warns against it. Users handle authentication and environment propagation because each CLI uses its own credentials and the deep-loop workflow does not mediate them. Runtime enforcement is out of scope.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-graph.md:75:If graph data says `STOP_BLOCKED`, the workflow emits a blocked-stop path and continues.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/README.md:73:This module is the coordination core beneath the runtime event spine. It prepares execution, protects write and lock boundaries, records evidence, repairs recoverable state and supplies the lifecycle and continuity signals consumed by reducers, recovery adapters and mode workflows.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-sealed-artifacts/README.md:17:Callers should use the exported API in `index.ts`. Filesystem, ledger and workflow policy remain owned by the shared runtime services.
