.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:19:Operator contract precedence for this skill surface (highest first): command entrypoint syntax in `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`; convergence math in `references/convergence/convergence.md` and the deep-research YAML workflow; runtime agent inventories from the checked-in runtime directories above.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:267:The YAML workflow owns executor selection (native `@deep-research` by default, or a routed CLI executor -- never ad hoc shell loops). Cross-CLI delegation inside an executor sandbox is possible but discouraged: do not invoke the same CLI from within itself, and do not assume auth propagates to child CLIs. The seven executor kinds are owned by `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`; the inline research YAML currently carries branches for `native`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-opencode`, and `cli-codex`, while `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, and `cli-pi` are handled by the shared fan-out adapters. Flag compatibility remains in [loop-protocol.md §3](references/protocol/loop-protocol.md).
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:303:`/deep:research` owns the YAML workflow: it initializes state, dispatches one LEAF iteration at a time, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `research/research.md`, and saves continuity. `@deep-research` executes only one research cycle per dispatch.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:319:Late-INIT can also anchor the research run to `spec.md`: the workflow acquires the advisory lock at `research/.deep-research.lock`, classifies `folder_state` (always one of `no-spec`, `spec-present`, `spec-just-created-by-this-run`, or `conflict-detected`), seeds or appends bounded context before LOOP, and replaces exactly one generated findings fence under the chosen host anchor during SYNTHESIS -- while keeping `research/research.md` canonical. The lock is held from late-INIT through save, skip-save, or cancel cleanup. Full marker syntax, audit events, and bounded mutation rules live in [spec-check-protocol.md](references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md).
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:340:9. **Treat research/research.md as workflow-owned** -- Iteration findings feed synthesis; the workflow owns the canonical `research/research.md`. The loop writes the file itself rather than scaffolding it through `create.sh --level research`, because its body is the synthesis of every iteration and only exists once the loop has run; `create.sh --level research` serves a research packet authored by hand
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:344:13. **Respect reducer ownership** -- The workflow reducer, not the agent, is the source of truth for strategy machine-owned sections, dashboard metrics, and findings registry updates
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:346:15. **Invoke through the command workflow** -- Use `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`, and let the YAML workflow own dispatch
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-improvement-common-sealed-artifacts/README.md:53:This folder owns the sealed artifacts step for Deep Improvement Common. It does not replace the shared substrate or decide consumer-facing workflow policy.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/ideas-backlog-lifecycle.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:3:description: "A finished fan-out research run now closes as complete, both research workflows honor --stop-policy=max-iterations and confirm mode has its quality guards back."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:13:A fan-out research run (one research topic split across several models, each running its own lineage) now closes as complete once its synthesis is written. Both research workflows also run to their ceiling when asked, and confirm mode checks quality again before it stops.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:22:- **`--stop-policy=max-iterations` holds in both workflows.** Auto and confirm now run to their iteration ceiling when asked. The rule is its own step, so the default convergence mode cannot skip it.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:23:- **Confirm mode has its quality guards back.** An earlier edit that aligned the two workflows dropped the quality checks from confirm's convergence step, so it could stop without them. They are back, and a test now holds each confirm workflow to its auto twin.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:24:- **The close-out runs from one shared script.** Both research workflows call the deep-loop runtime's close-out script, which also matches a finding by its `findingId` field.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/synthesis-save-and-guardrails/resource-map-emission.md:19:Operators need a scannable citation ledger after a long research loop. If the workflow only emits `research.md`, it is still hard to see which paths were repeatedly cited and which categories dominated the investigation.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/synthesis-save-and-guardrails/resource-map-emission.md:30:- Expected execution process: Inspect the docs and workflow first, then run the shared extractor or reducer emission path on representative deltas, then exercise the opt-out branch.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/synthesis-save-and-guardrails/resource-map-emission.md:32:- Expected signals: The synthesis workflow contains an emission step, the reducer supports `--emit-resource-map`, the shared extractor renders template categories with citation counts, and config opt-out skips cleanly.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/synthesis-save-and-guardrails/resource-map-emission.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so the workflow contract is checked before the direct emission path.
