.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:14:On the live path, `deep_loop_graph_upsert` and `deep_loop_graph_convergence` run in the auto and confirm workflows. Reducer-owned surfaces expose `graphConvergenceScore`, `graphDecision` and `graphBlockers`, while blocked-stop JSONL events appear in the findings registry, dashboard and strategy `next-focus` anchor.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:18:The workflow is meant to be easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:22:- **Blocked stops become recorded workflow events.** The `blocked_stop` event carries blocker and recovery context into reducers.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:37:Both research workflows emit a first-class `blocked_stop` JSONL event through `step_emit_blocked_stop`. Its `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy` and full session run history give downstream reducers the exact blocker and recovery context.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:43:At emission, `step_normalize_pause_events` maps raw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` to `userPaused` and `stuckRecovery` using the frozen `STOP_REASONS` enum. The live workflow no longer passes free-form strings into `synthesis_complete.stopReason`.
