.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.1.0.md:18:- **The two unsupported lifecycle modes are deferred.** When a research packet already existed, the workflow asked operators how to continue: `resume` the same run, start a fresh run, `fork` into a sibling run history, or use `completed-continue` to reopen a finished run after snapshotting its synthesis. The first two choices worked. `fork` and `completed-continue` had no workflow wiring and did the same thing as `resume` and quietly kept the old session id, so operators who thought they had branched a research run history ended up overwriting the original. `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, both loop-protocol references, both command workflows and the Claude Code and Codex agent definitions now mark the modes as deferred, while the normal happy path stays the same with `new`, `resume` and `restart` as the visible choices. The v1.5.0.0 changelog gained an append-only "Update (post-release)" block that points at this release.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:30:- Expected execution process: Inspect the loop protocol for Step 4a, then the state format dashboard section, then the dashboard template asset, then the YAML workflow step.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/dashboard-sparkline-trend.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/path-coverage-termination/README.md:3:description: "Evaluates whether a workflow mode has covered its required region universe well enough to terminate."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/path-coverage-termination/README.md:12:Runtime primitives that decide whether a `system-deep-loop` workflow mode has done enough work to stop. A frozen coverage universe is compiled per mode from major regions, dimensions and required evidence classes, a reducer folds path-coverage events into per-path state and the evaluator compares that projection against the universe and a coverage certificate to produce a termination decision. The result is currently shadow-only: it attaches proof diagnostics to the legacy graph-decision bridge without taking over authority.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/stop-when-all-key-questions-are-answered.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:924:// in-process dispatchSeat callback. A YAML-interpreted workflow cannot:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.8.0.0.md:12:Research iterations can now run through `codex exec` with a chosen model, reasoning effort and service tier instead of relying only on the native research agent with Claude Opus. The YAML workflow continues to own state tracking, convergence detection, lifecycle events and the reducer. The CLI runs inside that workflow, not as a replacement, and this release ships as a symmetric pair with `deep-review` v1.5.0.0.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/README.md:12:Runtime primitives that keep legacy JSON and JSONL readers fed while a `system-deep-loop` workflow mode migrates its state to the ledger. The engine folds verified ledger events into legacy-format bytes without acquiring legacy write authority. A durable shadow store publishes those bytes atomically with watermark tracking so refreshes never regress or partially overwrite a reader-visible file.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/iteration-reads-state-before-research.md:30:- Expected execution process: Inspect the workflow loop steps, then the quick reference iteration checklist, then the OpenCode runtime agent instructions for the single-iteration sequence.
