.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:16:The goal is to make the workflow easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:21:- **Canonical packet artifacts are aligned.** Skill docs, references, runtime mirrors and workflow assets carry the packet contract across those surfaces.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:42:Canonical `deep-research-*` packet artifacts are now frozen across the skill docs, references, runtime mirrors and workflow assets. `SKILL.md` freezes the lifecycle vocabulary, reducer ownership, lineage and runtime contract guidance, and the README reframes the skill around the canonical research-only packet model.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:50:OpenCode, Claude, Codex and the compatibility wrapper now describe the same deep-research packet expected behavior. The auto and confirm workflow YAML assets carry the same lifecycle, migration, registry and reducer expectations. The manual testing playbook now describes reducer-owned refresh behavior consistently in the root playbook and concrete iteration scenarios.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:34:1. Start from the operator-visible research workflow, not a synthetic command matrix.
