.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-sealed-artifacts/README.md:54:This folder owns the sealed artifacts step for Deep Review. It does not replace the shared substrate or decide consumer-facing workflow policy.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:2:title: "DR-033 -- Research graph-aware stop gate surfaces convergence verdict and workflow hooks"
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:3:description: "Verify that graph_convergence reducer fields render in registry and dashboard, and that the research auto workflow calls graph upsert plus convergence before the inline stop vote."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:7:# DR-033 -- Research graph-aware stop gate surfaces convergence verdict and workflow hooks
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:15:This scenario validates graph-aware stop-gate surfacing for `DR-033`. The objective is to verify that `graph_convergence` events become reducer-owned `graphConvergenceScore`, `graphDecision`, and `graphBlockers`, that the dashboard renders those graph signals, and that the live auto workflow invokes the graph tools before the inline 3-signal vote.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:19:Graph-aware stop logic only protects the loop if two things stay true at the same time: the reducer must surface the graph decision into operator-facing artifacts, and the live workflow must actually call the graph tools before evaluating the inline STOP candidate. If either side drifts, operators can no longer trust the graph-aware stop gate.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:27:- Title: Research graph-aware stop gate surfaces convergence verdict and workflow hooks.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:29:- When: The operator runs the reducer and inspects the live auto workflow definition.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:31:- Real user request: How do I know the research reducer is surfacing graph convergence output and that the autonomous workflow actually consults the graph before it decides to stop?
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:33:- Expected execution process: Run the reducer first to refresh generated artifacts, inspect the reducer-owned registry and dashboard second, then inspect the workflow YAML to verify the live graph-tool call order.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:34:- Desired user-visible outcome: The user gets a plain-language explanation that graph signals are visible in reducer outputs and that the autonomous workflow consults graph convergence before allowing inline STOP to become legal.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:36:- Pass/fail posture: PASS if graph signals appear in the registry and dashboard and the YAML shows the graph-tool calls in the pre-inline-vote path; FAIL if graph data is missing from any reducer surface or the workflow no longer calls the graph tools before the inline vote.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:46:3. Inspect registry, dashboard, and workflow YAML in that order so reducer outputs are verified before orchestration wiring.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:59:Registry surfaces `graphConvergenceScore`, `graphDecision`, and `graphBlockers`; dashboard renders `GRAPH CONVERGENCE`; workflow YAML calls both graph tools before the inline 3-signal vote.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:65:PASS if graph signals appear in the registry and dashboard and the workflow YAML still calls the graph tools in the graph-aware stop path; FAIL if graph data is missing from any reducer surface or the YAML no longer shows the graph-tool hooks.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:68:Privilege reducer-owned registry output for surfaced state and the workflow YAML for live orchestration order. If reducer fields exist but the YAML lacks graph-tool calls, treat that as graph-aware stop-gate wiring drift rather than a reducer regression.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/graph-aware-stop-gate.md:86:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` | Live research auto workflow; invokes `deep_loop_graph_upsert` and `deep_loop_graph_convergence` before the inline 3-signal vote |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:3:description: "Deep-research's graph work now has a peer skill of its own. The change gives its workflows a direct route to graph state instead of relying on a separate skill's MCP server."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:12:Deep-research's graph work now has a peer skill of its own. The change gives its workflows a direct route to graph state instead of relying on a separate skill's MCP server.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:18:Before arc 118, workflow steps that needed graph state passed through an MCP marshalling layer. The arrangement had accumulated drift with no ADR to justify it.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:46:Before arc 118, `deep_research_auto.yaml` and `deep_research_confirm.yaml` dispatched graph operations through tools registered with the spec-memory MCP server. Both workflows now invoke scripts directly for convergence, upsert, query and status, following the pattern already used by `reduce-state.cjs`.
