.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/anti-convergence-floor.md:27:The config template defines `antiConvergence.minIterations` with a default of `3` and `antiConvergence.convergenceMode` with a default of `default`. The auto workflow writes those values into the config record, validates older or malformed configs at read time, and clamps the effective floor to the hard `maxIterations` cap when needed.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/anti-convergence-floor.md:29:During convergence checking, a STOP candidate is blocked while the completed iteration count is below the effective floor. When the floor clears, the workflow emits `min_iterations_guard_pass`, keeping attribution separate from quality-guard events. `convergenceMode: "off"` disables convergence-driven STOP while leaving max iterations, pause, and other explicit halts active.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/changelog/v1.7.0.0.md:13:> Spec folder: `specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/028-confirm-mode-stop-hint` (Level 1)
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/stuck-detection.md:21:Stuck detection is the loop's way of noticing that research is circling. It prevents repeated low-value passes by moving the workflow into a recovery branch with a different angle.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/stuck-detection.md:27:The workflow computes `stuckCount` from the JSONL history. It increments the counter when an evidence iteration falls below the configured convergence threshold or self-reports `stuck`. `insight` resets the counter because a conceptual breakthrough still counts as progress, while `thought` is skipped because it is not evidence gathering.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:47:- Stdout is JSON-only for workflow-facing responses.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:153:- `/doctor:deep-loop` calls status, query and convergence with `--read-only`. Its route is `add-only` only because the workflow writes its packet-local state log.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:13:> Spec folder: `specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/027-stop-second-rater` (Level 1)
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/changelog/v1.5.1.0.md:22:- **One close-out for review and research.** `scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs` replaces the copies that the review and research workflows each carried inline. Where the copies disagreed it keeps the stricter rule, so review now refuses a symlinked artifact and research also matches a finding by its `findingId` field.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/quality-guards.md:27:The legal-stop bundle is explicit. After a stop nomination, the workflow checks that each key question has evidence-backed coverage, that research stayed aligned with the original question set, and that the answered set is not leaning on a single tentative source. A stop is legal only when both the convergence gate and these guard checks pass together.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/quality-guards.md:29:Guard failures are visible packet events, not quiet side effects. The workflow emits `guard_violation` lines for the specific issue and then persists a `blocked_stop` event with gate results, blocker names, recovery guidance, session identifier, and generation. The reducer uses those events to update next focus, blocked-stop history, and dashboard reporting for the next loop turn.
